# Security & Privacy

## Secrets
- No secrets in code, commits, logs, issues, PR descriptions or AI prompts. `.env` is git-ignored;
  only `.env.example` (names + dummy values + comment) is committed.
- Secrets live in: GitHub Environments (CI), Railway variables, or AWS Secrets Manager / SSM.
- Separate credentials per environment. Production keys are never used in develop/staging.
- If a secret is ever committed: treat it as leaked — rotate first, then clean history. Tell the human immediately.

## Authentication
- Passwords hashed with argon2id (or bcrypt cost ≥ 12). Never log or return hashes.
- Short-lived access tokens (≤ 15 min) + rotating refresh tokens stored server-side / httpOnly cookie.
- Rate-limit login, OTP, password reset and public forms. Lockout / captcha after repeated failures.
- 2FA available for admin roles.

## Authorization
- Default deny. Every route has an explicit guard (auth + role/permission + tenant).
- RBAC permissions checked in the service layer for sensitive actions, not only in the UI.
- Object-level checks: verify the resource belongs to the current tenant **and** the user may access it (prevent IDOR).

## Input / output
- Validate and whitelist all input. Parameterized queries only (ORM) — never string-concatenated SQL.
- Sanitize any user HTML (e.g. email/landing builders) with an allowlist sanitizer.
- File uploads: size + MIME allowlist, stored in object storage (S3/R2), never executed, served via signed URLs.
- Security headers via `helmet`; strict CORS allowlist per environment; CSRF protection for cookie auth.

## Webhooks (Meta, payment gateways, etc.)
- Verify signatures (e.g. `X-Hub-Signature-256` for Meta) using the raw body before parsing.
- Respond 200 fast, process asynchronously in a queue, dedupe by event ID.

## Dependencies
- Dependabot / Renovate enabled. `npm audit --audit-level=high` in CI. No abandoned packages for security-critical paths.

## Privacy — Israeli Protection of Privacy Law (incl. Amendment 13) & GDPR where relevant
- Collect the minimum personal data needed; document purpose for each PII field.
- PII is never written to logs, analytics events, error trackers or AI prompts unless required and masked.
- Support data export and deletion per data subject (per tenant).
- Access to production data is logged (audit log table: who, what, when, tenant).
- Marketing messages (WhatsApp/SMS/email) require recorded opt-in consent and a working opt-out
  (Israeli Communications Law "spam" section 30A). Store consent source + timestamp.
- Note: this is engineering guidance, not legal advice — flag compliance questions to the CTO.
